{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sugarcandy-fusible-hogget","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\n`process_snapshot` (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`) copies every key of a SNAPSHOT's\n`compiled_state` into reduced state, and ordinary replay starts at the latest SNAPSHOT.\nAny ticket compacted after a forced close was followed by reopen (bug 6df4-d3f0, fixed in\nthe reducer fold) has the stale `force_close_reason` / `close_class` / `close_reason` /\n`completion_expectation` frozen into its SNAPSHOT. Fixing the fold and bumping the reducer\ncache version does not reach these: replay never re-folds the retired source events.\n\n## Evidence (this repo's tracker, 2026-10-18)\n\n- 8 SNAPSHOTs with `status: closed`, a `force_close_reason`, and `last_reopened_at` set,\n  whose most recent closing STATUS event carried no force reason (e.g. aabf-d89e,\n  a8ea-be28, ad81-73ad, 3d7a-7795, 7332-a728, a881-2d9a, 52b0-6a6a, 14f4-d616).\n- 4 SNAPSHOTs with status open/in_progress still carrying `force_close_reason`\n  (76b2-4b5f, 075b-1479, 84e6-0fda, e215-ab23).\n\n## Approach to decide in plan review\n\n`rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py`) already\nrecomputes a SNAPSHOT from the full log including `*.retired` sources, under the write\nlock with a crash-safe sentinel. A one-shot idempotent migration in the ensure-registry\n(`docs/migrations.md`) could select tickets whose SNAPSHOT carries `force_close_reason`\nand `last_reopened_at` and rebuild them. This mutates the shared tracker, so it is split\nfrom the pure reducer fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every SNAPSHOT whose compiled close metadata disagrees with a full-log reduction is\n  rebuilt; a fixture store with a stale closed SNAPSHOT reduces with no `force_close_reason`.\n- [ ] The migration is idempotent (second run makes no writes).\n\n## Testing\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit -k snapshot_close_metadata -q\n```","id":"df72-d570-8c77-44d4","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Compacted SNAPSHOTs bake in stale force_close_reason from a pre-reopen forced close"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792361518962037693,"uuid":"e1494450-a954-4007-8479-429cb6b8e2aa"}